				<description>&lt;figure class=&#34;photo&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;picture&gt;&#xA;    &lt;source media=&#34;(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)&#34; srcset=&#34;http://localhost:1313/images/about/alex-crt-static.jpg&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;img src=&#34;http://localhost:1313/images/about/alex-crt.gif&#34; width=&#34;400&#34; height=&#34;400&#34; alt=&#34;Photo of Alexsandro with a glitch effect&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/picture&gt;&#xA;&lt;/figure&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;hello-you-can-call-me-alex-d&#34;&gt;Hello! You can call me Alex :D&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I&amp;rsquo;m Alexsandro, but everyone calls me Alex. Data Coordinator and Tech Lead at &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.impulsogov.org/&#34;&gt;ImpulsoGov&lt;/a&gt;, where I handle the Data Warehouse architecture, the data pipelines and the cloud infrastructure behind public health work.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Other technical interests: software architecture, event-driven systems, Rust, 3D printing and vintage hardware (mainly Game Boy Advance).&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;teacher&#34;&gt;Teacher&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I&amp;rsquo;ve been teaching for years, from basic programming to data engineering. If you run a tech education project and could use a hand, &lt;a href=&#34;https://linkedin.com/in/Alexsandr0x&#34;&gt;reach out on LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
